.TH JIZZCRAFT 1 "" "JizzCraft" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jizzcraft \- private, offline media viewer and library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jizzcraft
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
JizzCraft indexes images and videos in place, never modifies them, and makes no
network connection in the default build. See
.BR jizzcraft-cli (1)
for the scriptable interface to the same library.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Check codecs and folders and print how to fix what is missing.
.TP
.BI \-\-import " DIR"
Import a folder at startup.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " FILE"
Use this library database.
.TP
.BI \-\-tab " NAME"
Start on library, images, videos or favorites.
.TP
.BI \-\-cmd " NAME[=JSON]"
Run a registry command after startup (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " CODE"
Interface language: en fr es de it pt.
.TP
.B \-\-disguise
Launch as a neutral "Viewer" (window name, application ID, discreet mode).
.TP
.B \-\-portable
Keep database, config and cache in ./jizzcraft-data next to the executable.
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
Keep database, config and cache under DIR.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/jizzcraft
Library database.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jizzcraft
Settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/jizzcraft
Thumbnails (never written next to your media).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jizzcraft-cli (1)
